  return agent(`You are revising ${r.adr_id} at ${r.path} (project ${ROOT}, Godot 4.7.2 GDScript) after per-ADR engine and TD-ADR reviews and a cross-ADR adjudication of the Core tier. Autonomous mode: "Revise flagged items". Apply every BLOCKING finding and every ruling you own; align your references to rulings owned by other ADRs without taking over their decisions; apply non-blocking findings unless clearly wrong (decline with a reason). Do not apply rejected findings. Edit only this file (grep and bounded reads; whole-file reads over 40 KB are refused). Keep Status Proposed. Replace the pending Review Log line with a Review Log dated 2026-10-29 listing each finding/ruling id and what was done. Never run git; do not edit registries, GDDs or other ADRs.

${forAdr(id)}

Your original registry candidates (return the final set matching the revised ADR): ${JSON.stringify(r.registry_candidates)}
Your original GDD sync items (return the final set): ${JSON.stringify(r.gdd_sync)}`,
    { label: `revise:${r.adr_id}`, phase: 'Revise', schema: REVISE, model: 'sonnet', effort: 'high' })
}))).filter(Boolean)

phase('Confirm')
const confirm = await agent(`Review-only: do NOT edit any file. The Core ADRs were just revised:
${files}
(1) For each blocking finding and ruling below, is it applied in the current text? List unapplied ones (with ADR id). (2) Residual inconsistencies between the Core ADRs and against Foundation ADR-0001..0010 and docs/registry/architecture.yaml (interface names and signatures, block and id ownership, hook order, restore order, budgets, Depends On / Enables symmetry). Quote concretely. Read by section.
Blocking findings:
${blockingList.join('\n') || 'none'}
Rulings:
${rulings ? rulings.rulings.map(x => `${x.id} owner ${x.owner_adr}: ${x.amendment}`).join('\n') : 'none'}`,
  { label: 'confirm:core', phase: 'Confirm', schema: CONFIRM, model: 'sonnet', effort: 'high' })

phase('Registry')
const registryReport = await agent(`You are the single serial writer for two files in ${ROOT}. Autonomous mode, standing instruction to apply registry updates after review.
(1) Append these registry candidates to docs/registry/architecture.yaml following the file's header LAYOUT rules and each section's existing entry shape; append after the last entry of the section; for referenced_by_update add the ADR path to the named entry's referenced_by only; merge duplicates (both ADRs in referenced_by) and report them; never modify other fields. Then run bash .claude/scripts/registry.sh validate (all 0) and python -c "import yaml;yaml.safe_load(open('docs/registry/architecture.yaml',encoding='utf-8'))"; fix any layout error you introduced.
Candidates: ${JSON.stringify(revised.map(r => ({ adr: r.adr_id, items: r.registry_candidates })))}
(2) Append to production/session-logs/decision-log.md (append only) one section per ADR: "## 2026-10-29 — architecture-decision (ADR-NNNN, core-adrs workflow)" with each decision as **Decision point:** / **Options considered:** / **Chosen:** / **Reason:** / **Category:** architecture, plus one entry for the review ("Revise flagged items"; applied and declined ids) and one for the registry update.
Decisions: ${JSON.stringify([...authored.map(r => ({ adr: r.adr_id, stage: 'author', items: r.decisions })), ...revised.map(r => ({ adr: r.adr_id, stage: 'revise', items: r.decisions, applied: r.applied, declined: r.declined }))])}
Edit no other file. Never run git. Return a short plain-text report.`,
  { label: 'registry+log', phase: 'Registry', model: 'sonnet', effort: 'medium' })

return {
  authored: authored.map(r => ({ adr: r.adr_id, path: r.path, summary: r.summary, depends_on: r.depends_on, tr_coverage: r.tr_coverage, foundation_asks: r.foundation_asks })),
  verdicts: all.map(v => ({ adr: v.adr_id, verdict: v.verdict, blocking: v.findings.filter(f => f.blocking).length, total: v.findings.length })),
  rulings,
  revised: revised.map(r => ({ adr: r.adr_id, applied: r.applied.length, declined: r.declined, open_questions: r.open_questions })),
  gdd_sync: revised.map(r => ({ adr: r.adr_id, items: r.gdd_sync })),
  confirm,
  registryReport,
}

