{'adr': 'ADR-0012', 'verdict': 'CONCERNS (engine seat, Godot 4.7.2). One blocking finding (E1), a trivial snippet fix. The design is idiomatic for 4.7.2 and uses no deprecated or post-cutoff API.\n\nChecks that came out clean:\n- No `const` holds a constructed object. Only int constants appear (`RNG_*`, `HOOK_*`).\n- The 4.7 typed-return override rule does not apply: the hooks are bound `Callable`s, not overrides.\n- The 4.7 rule that packed-array element writes skip setters is harmless, because the Graph declares no setters.\n  - Probe on 4.7.2: `h.col[1] = 9` ran 0 setter calls; whole-array assignment ran 1.\n- Packed-array aliasing behaves as ADR-0011 § 6.2 states.\n  - A local alias sees member element writes.\n  - `duplicate()` isolates a snapshot from later member writes.\n  - `resize` on the member also resizes the alias, because they share one ref.\n  - Reassigning the member orphans the alias.\n- No Object-method name clash. Method names such as `set_section_dormant`, `set_valve`, `draw_air`, `enter` and `run` do not clash with Object, and no member is named get, set, free or call.\n- No project class name collides with a built-in class. GraphNode and GraphEdit exist as built-ins, but `GraphNode` only appears in ADR-0011\'s rejected Alternative 1.\n- `Dictionary` lookup treats `StringName` and `String` keys as equal, so the `after` edge dictionaries (`{&"id": ..., &"tolerates_stale": ...}`) are fine.\n- Int64 wraps silently on overflow. The ADR relies on its D.13 bounds, which is acceptable.\n\nThe "probed" claims are credible and were reproduced.\n- I re-ran `0012/probe.gd` on the mono 4.7.2 editor binary.\n  - Counters: 129,452,998,661 and 129,453,260,805, matching the ADR.\n  - Burst test: posmod 677.\n  - Insertion sort: 3.9, 33.6 and 42.2 µs at 16, 56 and 64 entries.\n  - Loops over 4,096 elements: direct 48.2 µs, indirect 77.5 µs, accumulate 136.7 µs, swap 74.9 µs.\n  - clampi adds about 19 µs per 4,096 calls.\n- I hand-checked the (a) and (b) arithmetic and it holds.\n- Caveats are in E3 and E5. The loop probes use function-local arrays, and the sort probe used `while` where the ADR mandates `for` with `break`.\n- Release-export behaviour, the S1 accessor cost and S3 remain UNVERIFIED, as the ADR itself says.', 'blocking': 1, 'total': 6}
