{'adr': 'ADR-0015', 'verdict': 'CONCERNS (engine review, Godot 4.7.2). No hard blocker. The core engine decisions hold up on 4.7.2 and need no changes:\n- no engine physics on any sim path;\n- id-sorted SoA columns held in PackedInt32Array and PackedInt64Array;\n- `@abstract` ports, including the one-line `@abstract class_name X extends RefCounted` form (probed to parse and instantiate);\n- the typed-return override rule, which the ADR already applies;\n- the packed-array element-write change, which the ADR does not rely on (probed: 0 setter calls).\n\nThree things need amendment before Accepted. A literal reading of the ADR yields a hot-path lint failure (E1), a non-compiling constant (E2), and a restore that silently wraps out-of-range int32 values (E3). A forward-reference mismatch with ADR-0014 is listed in cross_adr.\n\nProbe results (4.7.2.stable.mono, headless, in adr-probes/review-ADR-0015):\n- V1 reproduced: `bsearch` insertion index exact for 2^53+7, `insert`, `remove_at`, `duplicate()` independence, `b = a` aliasing.\n- V2 partly reproduced: truncating `/` and `posmod`. The literal -181/256 and -768/256 values were not re-run.\n- V3 reproduced: 2^23+1 round-trips through `Node2D.position`, 2^24+1 collapses to 16777216.\n- V4 (300,000-fixture equivalence) and V5 to V8 (GDScript cost, SoA versus records, release export, `reparent`) were not re-run by me. V8 is answered in cross_adr.\n- The 2.4 versus 23.8 microsecond figures are plausible: a bare packed-array read in a loop costs about 14 ns here.', 'blocking': 0, 'total': 10}
