export const meta = {
  name: 'core-adrs-followup',
  description: 'Apply Core-tier amendments and asks to each Foundation ADR (one writer per file), fix the 14 Core residuals (one serial writer), then serial registry merge + decision log',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Amend', detail: 'one Sonnet writer per Foundation ADR + one Core residual fixer', model: 'sonnet' },
    { title: 'Registry', detail: 'serial registry merge + decision log', model: 'sonnet' },
  ],
}
const ROOT = 'D:/the-synaptic-sea-2d'
const CORE = 'C:/Users/dasbl/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/D--the-synaptic-sea-2d/a5c30614-4e6e-4b6b-a781-54ec94879f80/scratchpad/ar/core'
const BASE = `Work in ${ROOT} (Godot 4.7.2 GDScript game design repo). ADRs are large: grep headings and read ranges (whole-file reads over 40 KB are refused); Edit with exact unique old_string. Never run git. Status stays Proposed. Core ADRs ADR-0011..0019 and ADR-0034 were authored and reviewed today (2026-10-29) in docs/architecture/.`
const OUT = { type: 'object', properties: { file: { type: 'string' }, applied: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, declined: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: { ask: { type: 'string' }, reason: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['ask', 'reason'] } }, needs_user: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } }, required: ['file', 'applied', 'declined', 'needs_user'] }

phase('Amend')
const tasks = args.foundation.map(f => () => agent(`${BASE}

Edit ONLY docs/architecture/${f.file} (${f.adr}). Read ${CORE}/asks-${f.adr}.json: amendments requested by the Core ADR authors (from_adr) and by the Core-tier technical-director adjudication (from_adr "ADJUDICATED (binding)").
- Apply every ADJUDICATED item.
- For each author ask: read the requesting Core ADR's relevant section and this ADR's section; apply it if it is consistent with this ADR's decisions and does not weaken an existing guarantee (a clarification, an added name/row/entry, an exemption scoped as asked). Decline with a reason if it contradicts a decision here or is already covered (cite the line). If it would change a decision of this ADR substantively (behaviour, ownership, a budget), do not apply it: put it in needs_user with a one-line summary.
- Merge duplicate asks. Keep this ADR's style; add each change to its Review Log (or Amendments for ADR-0003) as one dated bullet "2026-10-29 Core-tier amendments" listing what was applied and the requesting ADR.
Return applied, declined and needs_user.`, { label: `amend:${f.adr}`, phase: 'Amend', schema: OUT, model: 'sonnet', effort: 'high' }))
tasks.push(() => agent(`${BASE}

You are the single writer for the Core ADRs (docs/architecture/adr-0011..0019-*.md and adr-0034-*.md); edit only those. Read ${CORE}/residuals.json: 14 residual inconsistencies left after the Core tier's confirm pass. For each, decide the correct form from the decision owner's text (the ADR whose scope owns the thing: e.g. the Graph RNG id field is ADR-0012's, section_contains frame is ADR-0013's, beam Light2D ownership follows the adjudicated CT rulings cited in the ADRs' Review Logs) and edit every involved ADR so they agree. For Depends On / Enables asymmetries, make each Enables row list exactly the ADRs (Foundation or Core) that list it under Depends On (hard deps only; soft/related/validation rows are not Depends On). Add one dated Review Log bullet per edited ADR ("2026-10-29 confirm residuals"). Return applied (one line per residual), declined, needs_user.`, { label: 'residuals:core', phase: 'Amend', schema: OUT, model: 'sonnet', effort: 'high' }))
const amended = await parallel(tasks)

phase('Registry')
const reg = await agent(`${BASE}

You are the single serial writer for docs/registry/architecture.yaml and production/session-logs/decision-log.md; edit only those two files.
Read ${CORE}/registry-work.json: "candidates" (registry entries proposed by the 10 Core ADRs after review: section, name, entry_yaml) and "decisions" (author and revise decisions per ADR).
(1) Before appending each candidate, check it against the CURRENT text of its ADR (grep the name/signature), because the Core ADRs and Foundation ADRs were amended after the candidates were drafted; adjust the entry to the current ADR text. Follow the registry header LAYOUT rules and each section's existing entry shape; append after the last entry of its section; for section referenced_by_update add the ADR path to the named entry's referenced_by only; merge duplicates (list every ADR in referenced_by). Then run bash .claude/scripts/registry.sh validate (all counts 0) and python -c "import yaml;yaml.safe_load(open('docs/registry/architecture.yaml',encoding='utf-8'));print('ok')"; fix any layout error.
(2) Append to production/session-logs/decision-log.md (append only) one section per ADR: "## 2026-10-29 — architecture-decision (ADR-NNNN, core-adrs workflow)" with each decision as **Decision point:** / **Options considered:** / **Chosen:** / **Reason:** / **Category:** architecture, plus one entry for the review ("Revise flagged items": applied and declined ids) and one entry for this registry update.
Return a short plain-text report: entries added per section, merges, adjustments made against current ADR text, validate output, sections appended.`, { label: 'registry+log', phase: 'Registry', model: 'sonnet', effort: 'medium' })
return { amended, reg }

